cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  CFMOSCPTCS — A Computational Framework for Modeling and Optimization of
  Sensor-Constrained Powertrain Torque Control Systems
message: >-
  If you use or reference this project, please cite it using the metadata
  below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Avishek
    family-names: Barua
repository-code: https://github.com/avishekb798/cfmoscptcs
abstract: >-
  A simulation-based computational framework that models a simplified
  powertrain torque control system, injects five types of realistic sensor
  imperfections (noise, bias, drift, sampling rate limitations, and signal
  delay) into the feedback loop, measures the resulting performance
  degradation through RMS error, overshoot, and settling time, and uses
  grid search optimization across 16,807 configurations to identify optimal
  sensor configurations. Developed as a senior design project at California
  State University, Dominguez Hills.
keywords:
  - powertrain
  - torque control
  - PID controller
  - sensor imperfections
  - grid search optimization
  - simulation framework
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-05-08"
